# Background theory for the GeoNames slice: France and Germany declared
# distinct.
#
# GeoNames publishes no distinctness.  The parties declare that the two
# country features name different countries.  This settles identity
# questions (KGC304) but not containment: two distinct areas can still lie
# one within the other (KGC305).

@prefix bt:      <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/background#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/geonames-europe/declared> a bt:BackgroundTheory ;
    dcterms:title "France and Germany declared distinct"@en ;
    bt:generatedBy bt:PartyDeclaration ;
    bt:appliesTo <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/geonames-europe> ;
    bt:pairCount 1 .
